{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages","id":1555207,"title":"What would you think of this Cabal of Mages?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-07T09:45:43-08:00","id":1555207,"title":"What would you think of this Cabal of Mages?","content":"The Group is composed of member of the Verbena, a Dreamspeaker, a member of the Cult of Ecstasy, a Euthanatos and a member of the Akashic Brotherhood. The Verbena mage and Dreamspeaker have found allies among the Garou due to similar worldviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-07-2025, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T10:08:57-08:00","id":1555209,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think very much. Just based on Tradition, there's not much to say.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Euthanatoi and the Aksashics have a tradition of hating each other... But lots of them don't.<br /> <br /> There's no Hermetic, Chorister, Etherite, or Adept. That's suggestive of a certain perspective on the world... But it'd be trivially easy to be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T11:26:28-08:00","id":1555212,"title":"","content":"There's not much to say. It looks like your average Cabal.<br /> <br /> Two observations: <hr /><br /> Maybe the most polemical thing it's that the Verbena and Dreamspeaker &quot;have found allies among the Garou due to similar worldviews&quot;.<br /> <br /> Garou dislike of mages has very little to do with having philosophical discrepancies, and a lot to do with deeply ingrained prejudice.<br /> <br /> In general trying to ally with Garou requires being incredibly close to their culture from the get-go (Easiest way of having that: the Kinfolk Merit ). Being successfull otherwise implies you've miraculously managed to avoided the minefield that it's Garou paranoia <i>w/o even knowing there's one in the first place</i>. Sharing a similar worldview (whatever that means) helps very little with that, and may even make things <i>worse</i>.<br /> <br /> Because, from the perspective of the Garou <i>worldview</i>, mages have no business <i>existing</i> in the first place (or, well, doing magick instead of accepting the laws of the world like good apes should). Humans having magick it's a mistake, it's <i>fucked up</i>. For some Garou, mages communing with the spirits and respecting Gaia it's the <i>least </i>they can do if they insist in using dangerous powers they shouldn't be using. So, sharing such a worldview may appease them a little. But for other Garou, that's even <i>worse </i>because communing with spirits it's <i>their</i> divine right and not of humans.<br /> <br /> Unless - of course - the ST it's willing to ignore all the potential problems present in the Lore in favor of a &quot;nature-lovers together strong&quot; sort of narrative ... then all I have said does not matter at all <hr /><br /> Euthanatos and the Brotherhood had an old feud, but it's mostly water under the bridge now since that war happened centuries ago (unless they have Past Lives that have something to say about that, or their mentors are/were related to the war)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-07-2025, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T12:52:47-08:00","id":1555214,"title":"","content":"Well, some Garou Tribes allow Kinfolk to use Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T13:08:54-08:00","id":1555215,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that (1) in-universe Numina are not widely acknowledged as a single phenomenon, or small set of related ones, the practices Garou tolerate Kinfolk to study are seen as traditional Kin practices and thus are limited compared to the full list out there and (2) that is heavily swayed by the two Kinfolk books, which are both very clear that the options presented for playable Kinfolk are exceptional by the default of the game to make Kin more interested PCs rather than override the &quot;standard&quot; that most Kin operate under.<br /> <br /> All that said, the original question of the thread is still impossible to answer because you haven't presented a cabal. Just a list of affiliations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T14:49:24-08:00","id":1555217,"title":"","content":"Well, I was just posting a concept but I did think of something for at least two of them motive wise. The Verbena mage thinks that the Garou and other shapeshifters are somehow tied to the Wyck and the Dreamspeaker of course has the interest of fighting the Wyrm. in regards to Spheres however, the Verbena mage uses the spheres of life, spirit, prime and entropy. The Dreamspeaker focuses on life, spirit, correspondence, matter and prime. The Akashic Brother focuses on life, spirit, correspondence, matter and mind. And the Euphanatos focuses on life, spirit, time and entropy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T15:45:55-08:00","id":1555220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555212#post1555212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou dislike of mages has very little to do with having philosophical discrepancies, and a lot to do with deeply ingrained prejudice.</div> </div> </div> </div>The things you presented, while real, are far from a rule among Garou. They don't even understand Sphere Magic nearly enough to have a strong opinion on it as a general thing, or to understand they're all the &quot;same thing&quot; to begin with. So, many will find the ideas of humans wielding such powers abhorrent, but many won't have a strong opinion one way or the other.<br /> <br /> But that said, they <b>are</b> overall very paranoid, <b><i>and frequently with reason</i></b>. Mages in particular pose another, more pragmatic threat to them: they drain Caerns. Caerns are powerful Nodes, and even like-minded Mages frequently don't understand their place and importance for Garou society, or for the world at large under Garou POV.<br /> <br /> Now, that said, some Traditions <b>do</b> have a history of alliances with the Garou, so it isn't completely far-fetched, although it would need more elaboration upon.<br /> <br /> Either way, any Mage working with Garou would be well advised to keep a wide berth from Caerns at all costs, never even <i>mention</i> approaching one, and if you ever get near one by any reason, even helping to save or recover it, first order of the day is to get away A.S.A.P.. And never, never, never, <b>NEVER</b> take any Quint from a Caern for any purpose, through any means.<br /> <br /> Also, any Fetish found that was made by Shapechangers or owned by them is theirs, and treat it as sacred before delivering, because it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555217#post1555217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I was just posting a concept but I did think of something for at least two of them motive wise. The Verbena mage thinks that the Garou and other shapeshifters are somehow tied to the Wyck and the Dreamspeaker of course has the interest of fighting the Wyrm. in regards to Spheres however, the Verbena mage uses the spheres of life, spirit, prime and entropy. The Dreamspeaker focuses on life, spirit, correspondence, matter and prime. The Akashic Brother focuses on life, spirit, correspondence, matter and mind. And the Euphanatos focuses on life, spirit, time and entropy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who are those people? How old are them? What they believe in? Why are they together, and why they belong to their respective group? What they do for a living? How they behave? What's special about them or about the group (special isn't necessarily powerful or important, &quot;fantasizes about being a jedi since childhood&quot; is special enough).<br /> <br /> A list of Traditions and Spheres isn't something we can think anything about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T07:55:59-08:00","id":1555240,"title":"","content":"I haven't decided yet on how exactly they would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T09:41:07-08:00","id":1555243,"title":"","content":"While the <b>Kinfolk</b> Merit is useful for these characters we should also remember the <b>Supernatural Ally </b>merit. The second merit implies a certain level of trust and alliance.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if you're going this route have the Garou allies have their own ideas and goals. After all, if the Garou allies have some awareness of the capacities of Mages, then they might want practical help. Mages could use their abilities to get information for the Garou that's either unavailable or brutally hard to get for Garou. Mages could cause Pentex equipment to short out at the best times for Garou. Wards against Black Spiral Dancers that give Gaian Garou the edge. Garou would be delighted to get favors. A little harder to get favors from, but delighted to receive. ;-)<br /> <br /> Going in the opposite direction. I once ran a Werewolf campaign were a powerful local Hermetic had reasons to hate Pentex, or at least the local branch. He offered the Garou bits of Intel and made useful accidents happen on cue. The Garou Elders gave the PCs hell for the Mage interfering, but they accepted the results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 11-08-2025, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T13:17:25-08:00","id":1555245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555243#post1555243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the <b>Kinfolk</b> Merit is useful for these characters we should also remember the <b>Supernatural Ally </b>merit. The second merit implies a certain level of trust and alliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a purely mechanical standpoint, I'd say this is more important than anything else.<br /> <br /> In my current Mage game one of the PCs has good-ish relations with the Garou. Good-ish because he's married to one, but for game effects the husband is an Enemy because he is overprotective with the kinfolk PC and frequently comes to take him back home.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555243#post1555243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages could cause Pentex equipment to short out at the best times for Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets just remember that Pentex isn't seen as a threat by every Garou, much less by those who would likely ally to your run-of-the-mill Verbena and Dreamspeaker.<br /> <br /> Pentex isn't a general Garou problem, it's a Glasswalker problem. Most Werewolves are likely to run into their business, but never learn about the corporation behind it as Pentex works through subsidiaries with their own subsidiaries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555240#post1555240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't decided yet on how exactly they would be like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Share your thought process, then, what made you choose this number of Mages, this particular spread of Traditions, and anything else you already have in mind about them, even if not yet a fixed decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T19:39:45-08:00","id":1555260,"title":"","content":"Well, the Dreamspeaker was because they had a similar animistic worldview as well as a history of working with the Garou I also thought they could be Kinfolk, I chose the Verbena Mage because I figured what if they saw the Garou as connected to the Wyck somehow and so they try to get on good terms with them the Verbena tradition also has a history of working with the Garou. I picked the Cult of Ecstasy, the Euthanatos and Akashic Brotherhood traditions because I felt that they would probably find some common ground with their respective paradigms. I also decided that maybe the Dreamspeaker, Verbena Mage and Cult of Ecstasy Mage all use a lot of herbalism in their magic so they find some common ground there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-09-2025, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T19:43:47-08:00","id":1555261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555209#post1555209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't think very much. Just based on Tradition, there's not much to say.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Euthanatoi and the Aksashics have a tradition of hating each other... But lots of them don't.<br /> <br /> There's no Hermetic, Chorister, Etherite, or Adept. That's suggestive of a certain perspective on the world... But it'd be trivially easy to be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you have in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T11:02:22-08:00","id":1555274,"title":"","content":"The unrepresented Traditions are the two former Technocracy members and two also-rans of the Technocracy. So it's perhaps suggestive of a cabal that is paranoid of Technocratic subversion to the extent that they're even suspicious of individuals who are even dimly related? Or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T12:42:33-08:00","id":1555281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555260#post1555260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Dreamspeaker was because they had a similar animistic worldview as well as a history of working with the Garou I also thought they could be Kinfolk, I chose the Verbena Mage because I figured what if they saw the Garou as connected to the Wyck somehow and so they try to get on good terms with them the Verbena tradition also has a history of working with the Garou. I picked the Cult of Ecstasy, the Euthanatos and Akashic Brotherhood traditions because I felt that they would probably find some common ground with their respective paradigms. I also decided that maybe the Dreamspeaker, Verbena Mage and Cult of Ecstasy Mage all use a lot of herbalism in their magic so they find some common ground there.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you have an overall idea of a common paradigm between them, good.<br /> <br /> What's this paradigm like? It may seem quite obvious in your head, but it isn't, the game is actually extremely flexible in how a specific Mage's paradigm is regardless of Tradition. So, what are the things they believe and practice that are so common? How <b>they</b> define those similarities, and why they're relevant to them?<br /> <br /> Most important, why that makes them <i>want</i> to be a cabal and what they plan on achieving together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T07:48:38-08:00","id":1555310,"title":"","content":"Their paradigms focus a lot on spirituality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T10:51:24-08:00","id":1555322,"title":"","content":"We need a little more than that ... :P<br /> <br /> Is it a cabal interested in <i>figthing spiritual corruption</i>?. Is it more of a <i>reseach </i>Cabal that's interested in the spirit wilds?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I figured what if they saw the Garou as connected to the Wyck somehow</div> </div> </div> </div>The HOW it's kinda important here. There's many angles in &quot;how&quot; they could be related that can colour the relationship.<br /> <br /> But in any case, linking Garou with the origins of magic(k) it's something of an interesting belief. <hr /><b>A weird unconventional idea </b>I had when thinking about how Garou legends and magic(k):<br /> <br /> Maybe the Dreamspeaker was taught how to control magick not by humans, initially, but by a Garou Ally and/or by a Spirit related to the tribe (sometimes spirits like to poach mages that are about to awaken - there's a whole camp of the Dreamspeakers based arround this). Of course, this would produce an unorthodox mage, but could also give interesting perspectives. One of the myths of the Garou about magic(k) talks about the original mages stealing their power from the great spirits (that's also a very common idea in many myths: Humanity stealing from the gods), they could've been educated into this.<br /> <br /> Verbena know the Wyck as half-human half-something that were the first to use magick, and mages are their legacy. Spirits/gods it's a possible source for the other half. There are a lot of concepts about how Gods could have mixed with humanity. Maybe humans made a deal to marry with the gods and have these children. If being sensationalist, one could say, the ancient humans seduced the gods to gain their power- and that would be relatable to the Garou mythos. Maybe mages are a a bit of &quot;half-spirit&quot; themselves.<br /> <br /> Extatics, Euhanatos and Akashick are known for scouring the past trough past lives and the Dream. Depending on their beliefs, they could be compatible with the idea of their divergent paths of magick coming as a result of connecting with a big &quot;other&quot;, be it divine or enlightened.<br /> <br /> So, the Cabal could be joined to navigate the spiritual realms of history (the collective dream, the wheel of reincarnation), to find traces of this &quot;missing link&quot; of WHOM did the ancestors of mages meet to gain their legacy.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> This <b>crazy</b> idea it's just to show a <i><b>seed</b> </i>for a Cabal that I could imagine going to be &quot;out there&quot; and doing things. That could have enemies other than Banes and &quot;Pentex&quot; (or it's subsidiary subsidiaries, as we all know, :P ), maybe history-spirits and past-lives/ancestor spirits, that either don't aprove the goal, or just ward the deepest recesses of history from trespassers, could be their particular antagnoists.<br /> A Cabal that's maybe peacefull but &quot;figthing&quot; would still easily happen as consequence of &quot;being a mage&quot;, and trying to live and learn, and get the resources and mojo for lasting journeys to the far reaches of the Umbra. And that before thinking about the enemies of the Garou that are going to come along with the Ally or the spirit mentor. <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets just remember that Pentex isn't seen as a threat by every Garou, much less by those who would likely ally to your run-of-the-mill Verbena and Dreamspeaker.<br /> Pentex isn't a general Garou problem, it's a Glasswalker problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD Lore always &quot;allies&quot; same with same: shamans with shamans, techies with techies, etc...But of all Garou I think Glasswalker have the best chance to have allies among many factions of Mages, because they can meet on the Web on a &quot;neutral ground&quot; (the Spy's Demise) that can be accessed from any place on the planet, by anyone (even sleepers, you don't need to be a technomancer), where them and mages of all the factions explicitly go to (carefully) exchange information.<br /> <br /> And that sounds to me like a more solid building for creating lasting relationships in the midst of almost cold-war paranoia than any other I've read about so far.<br /> <br /> But, of course, only technomancers care about the DigiWeb - although it's not at all necessary to be a technomancer to use it, mystical mages typically <i>do not</i>. Distrusting technology it's not unreasonable considering Technocrats.<br /> <br /> It could be cool if there were similar &quot;neutral grounds&quot; on the Umbra for more mystical types to talk, but if there's something WoD never cared to elaborate about, except for glossing over the most passing commonalities (such as having a punctual common threath), it's to <i>explore</i> <b><i>how this so called &quot;history of alliances&quot; actually happens</i> <i>in practice</i>.</b><br /> <br /> Or at least that's my impression. But I disgress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-10-2025, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T11:06:28-08:00","id":1555324,"title":"","content":"Well, I did think that they could be focused on fighting spiritual corruption and that they'd all have an interest in the Umbra. So your idea is pretty good, I was also thinking of the possibility that the Verbena Mage thinks the Garou and similar creatures are the Wyck or at least descended from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-10-2025, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T12:46:57-08:00","id":1555326,"title":"","content":"Well, to figth evil spirits it's almost always reasonable. But if that's the <i>main</i> <i>focus </i>of the Cabal ... a Cabal focused on <i>figthing </i>, or a War Cabal, something typically comes on two types:<br /> <br /> Either it's offensive: Maybe they're hunting a specific strong or vast enemy that's important for everyone, but none of the mages could hope to beat alone. Or they could be a Cabal mages w/o Spirit calls to deal with spiritual problems (Who You Gonna Call?)<br /> <br /> Or it's defensive. The Cabal it's focused on defending a place/region that for some reason atracts evil spirits. Maybe the place it's sacred or important and bad guys want to corrupt it - it just has to not be a Caern, otherwise Garou aren't going to be allies. Or maybe it's a bad place, an ancient evil happened there, or it's sealed there, and needs to be cleansed and protected from the forces that would unleash the evil<br /> <br /> The later may be easier to set up because it follows the traditional &quot;City&quot; model of Vampire/WoD (that is, it's a cabal centered on a place)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-10-2025, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T14:09:52-08:00","id":1555330,"title":"","content":"I guess they could be a Cabal that deals with things like Marauders, Nephandi and evil or out of control spirits. That idea of them providing spiritual services also sounds pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T15:45:22-08:00","id":1555337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555322#post1555322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WoD Lore always &quot;allies&quot; same with same: shamans with shamans, techies with techies, etc...But of all Garou I think Glasswalker have the best chance to have allies among many factions of Mages, because they can meet on the Web on a &quot;neutral ground&quot; (the Spy's Demise) that can be accessed from any place on the planet, by anyone (even sleepers, you don't need to be a technomancer), where them and mages of all the factions explicitly go to (carefully) exchange information.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree, but this doesn't seems to be what this cabal is about. If they're tech savvy enough (which is perfectly doable), then sure, but your &quot;regular&quot; (as far as that exists) <b>Verbena</b> or <b>Dream Speaker</b> won't really thread the areas where the <b>Glass Walkers</b> wander. They're more likely to meet other tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T06:33:40-08:00","id":1555358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555330#post1555330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess they could be a Cabal that deals with things like Marauders, Nephandi and evil or out of control spirits. That idea of them providing spiritual services also sounds pretty good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, those are very different kinds of trouble. Any mage could end having to face those treaths if found, but actually being <i>about </i>that it's very different.<br /> <br /> Cabals that fight Nephandi tend to be like &quot;secret police&quot;, hunting such corruption cannot be done oppenly because most Nephadi are infiltrated within the sects. A Cabal that offers spiritual services could end figthing Nephandi, and a cabal that hunts Nephandi would do well being able to fend off spirits. But these aren't the same <i>vocations</i>, so to speak<br /> <br /> (I <i>guess</i> you could have your cake and eat it if offering spiritual services it's a <i>front </i>to actually spy mages - but then, what happens if the service isn't needed, or wanted?. In any case, such a Cabal would be much more about dealing with information than with spirits or the Umbra)<br /> <br /> And Marauders are a &quot;case by case&quot; scenario. Traditions don't really go after them unless they're causing trouble, or attracting trouble. Some Marauders are subtler w/o being disruptive, and may even be considered allies. The Traditions aren't against Marauders any more than they are against rogue mages that are too noisy, dangerous or otherwise problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-11-2025, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T06:50:51-08:00","id":1555359,"title":"","content":"On the flip side, fighting spiritual corruption might be something they do to pay the bills and gather favors and connections while they pursue their real goals. That would let you have more of a generic approach to fighting said corruption. Then you just have to figure out what their main goal is. Or personal goals. It could also be that they all have different driving goals, and they are a team to help each other out with said goals and for pooling resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T10:14:44-08:00","id":1555636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555220#post1555220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that said, they <b>are</b> overall very paranoid, <b><i>and frequently with reason</i></b>. Mages in particular pose another, more pragmatic threat to them: they drain Caerns. Caerns are powerful Nodes, and even like-minded Mages frequently don't understand their place and importance for Garou society, or for the world at large under Garou POV.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean, do like-minded mages drain Caerns? In the MtAs books, nodes are always treated as priceless resources, with mages that drain nodes usually being considered extremely irresponsible or straight-up Nephandic. Likewise, has anyone seen a game where Council mages were stupid enough to try to steal a Caern? It's a stereotype, probably caused by some Nephandi if it ever happened at all, that is inconsistent with the worldview of the Council and Crafts as presented in MtAs books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26432,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","user":"JagneStormskull","date":". 11-19-2025, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T12:25:39-08:00","id":1555639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555636#post1555636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, do like-minded mages drain Caerns? In the MtAs books, nodes are always treated as priceless resources, with mages that drain nodes usually being considered extremely irresponsible or straight-up Nephandic. Likewise, has anyone seen a game where Council mages were stupid enough to try to steal a Caern? It's a stereotype, probably caused by some Nephandi if it ever happened at all, that is inconsistent with the worldview of the Council and Crafts as presented in MtAs books.</div> </div> </div> </div>imo you don't need a Nephandi plot for it to make sense. You have one side from whose perspective 99% of Craft Mages around Caerns play by the rules and are save. You have the other side who has seen the 1% failure rate cause catastrophic loss with immeasurable impact.<br /> A nuclear reactor meltdown has a vanishingly low risk of happening, and one side says the benefits outweigh that risk. The other side says the impact of when it happens outweighs the benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T12:46:50-08:00","id":1555641,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've sort of wondered about this myself. I don't think it's common at all for mages to deliberately damage a place of power. One could argue that maybe happened a few times and this is Garou Oral Tradition doing it's job (of preserving grudges).<br /> <br /> BUT there's a different way of looking at this: <hr />1rst. One has to remember a Caern it's more than a Node - it's a supernatural ecosystem, and a place of social and religious significance<br /> <br /> Sure, most mages won't drain Quintessence to the point of damaging a supernatural place, but they DO drain the &quot;free flowing&quot; Quintessence emanating of such places, and take the Tas. And maybe that's all &quot;<b>draining</b>&quot; means.<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% sure if taking a small portion of the free-flowing Quintessence of a Caern <i>damages</i> the Caern or not. I haven't found rules on that, tho I'm sure there were rules somewhere. Sure, Garou do this, sort off, when they regain Gnosis. But Caerns have their own properties on top of that. And maybe tampering with it using magicks could damage it's supernatural nature somehow.<br /> <br /> But let's say it <i>doesn't </i>damage the Caern.<br /> <br /> Caerns are incredibly sacred beyond their &quot;properties&quot; or &quot;utility&quot;. Garou wouldn't even let <i>normal</i> <i>kinfolk </i>enter the Caern itself. Imagine if they're going to tolerate people going there and taking small rocks and stuff like careless tourists . Of course they're not going to let you smoke the place's Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Even if it was harmless, it's incredibly offensive for the Garou, and for the Spirits that made deals with the Garou. <hr /><br /> 2nd. Mages definitely do tap into Nodes in more agressive ways.<br /> <br /> Technocrats would always &quot;sanitize&quot; a node before sitting on top of it. And that can't be good for the health of the Caern. Connecting a Node to a Realm would permanently drain part of it, and could also be problematic for the whole spirit ecology of the place. Of course Nephandi would wreck the place.<br /> <br /> Werewolf stories don't talk about this, specifically ... but then, I think Garou don't need nor want to know how Mages actually have developped a plethora of different ways to wreck or defile a caern. :P<br /> <br /> It's enough to know that they DO :P <hr /><br /> 3rd. Garou don't know enough about magic(k) to know if this horribly disrespectful request is or isn't harmless.<br /> <br /> Mages are the only splat that can process any and all supernatural power into Prime. The way others see it, you're taking what makes the place &quot;special&quot; and leaving nothing. Even <i>Demons </i>are unnerved by mages draining the &quot;holly&quot; out of a place<br /> <br /> Sure, you can say &quot;this ain't permanent, this is no different than when you guys do it&quot;. But they can't know if what you're doing it's actually harmless. And they aren't going to know until it's too late to do anything about it. <hr />So:<br /> <br /> Garou aren't going to be open to the idea this is harmless (even if it was). They're paranoid, and the stories about human mages aren't helping<br /> <br /> But <i>even if they were</i>, it's still bad because it's their holly place and of their spirits. It would be the difference between you politely asking if you can burn the church with the community inside, and politely asking if you can take a piss on the church and the churchgoers instead ... Either way, it's not a great way to start a conversation with someone already predisposed to think the worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-19-2025, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T12:46:57-08:00","id":1555642,"title":"","content":"It's also worth considering that from a WtA perspective, Caerns are tied to a specific location, while from a Mage perspective Nodes can be relocated. A lot of &quot;Caern draining&quot; could by more like redirecting a river to move a dam into a more advantageous position rather than ruining the headwaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T17:37:40-08:00","id":1555649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555636#post1555636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, do like-minded mages drain Caerns? In the MtAs books, nodes are always treated as priceless resources, with mages that drain nodes usually being considered extremely irresponsible or straight-up Nephandic. Likewise, has anyone seen a game where Council mages were stupid enough to try to steal a Caern? It's a stereotype, probably caused by some Nephandi if it ever happened at all, that is inconsistent with the worldview of the Council and Crafts as presented in MtAs books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking everything the others said above, and want to add a few more:<br /> <br /> 1. Mages are interventionists by nature, even when they don't see what they're doing as intervention. They think they know better and have an innate power that literally validates this thinking. While a given Mage can certainly stop themselves from interfering for diplomatic reasons, they <b>do</b> think they have better ideas on how to deal with this sacred place, and very little regard for what others think. And not few of them will act upon their ideas sooner or later if they think they have an opportunity;<br /> <br /> 2. Even like-minded Mages don't necessarily have the exactly same worldview of the Garou, especially because <b>the Garou</b> also think themselves overly special. The simple idea of a non-shapechanger thinkering with the Caern in any way whatsoever isn't simply a risk, it pushes their buttons in all kinds of ways, in so many levels, because they're sure not only that this is a sacred place, but that they're the sacred race worthy of it and tasked with its care, them and no one else. They <i>barely</i> accept non-Garou shapechangers in the best days;<br /> <br /> 3. Not all Tradition Mages are that careful by a long shot. Like-minded Mages may agree that the Caern is a sacred place, but most Mages aren't like-minded, they're sympathetic at best. And with their &quot;know better&quot; attitude, a lot is far more pragmatic than respectful when push comes to shove, especially if it is to defend a cause they think worth it, which isn't necessarily in line with Garou perspective. Sure, only a <i>Nefandus</i> would destroy a Caern for no good reason, but far more Mages have reasons they disagree with Werewolves on how good they are.<br /> <br /> 4. Add to 3 that Garou are straight-up heroes, even if flawed ones, in the sense that they live to fight an undeniable evil over the world, but this evil is only undeniable in their eyes. Mages are <i><b>not</b></i> necessary heroes and <i><b>a lot</b></i> of them are not good people. Being a <i>Nefandus</i> means serving directly the kind of Evil the Garou fight, but below that anything goes and there are even Tradition Mages that are every bit the stereotyped luddite psychopathic asshole the Technocracy paints them. A lot of Tradition Mages do abhorrent things just because they don't think it that bad and don't really have to be good people anyways. Destroying a Caern is well within what many of them would do because they think they have better uses for that energy and Garou religion be damned;<br /> <br /> 5. Other Nodes exist, many others. There's zero need for the Garou to have their allies near the Caern or for those allies to ask. The mere fact of a Mage asking this would be reason to raise red flags far more than grant any privileges. Just why you want it? Under very extreme circumstances the Garou may invite them if it is to help with defending the Caern against certain destruction or a similarly extreme task, and even then only if they trust those Mages a lot and have reason to really think they may need this help (endangering the Caern out of pride is still its own crime), but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Even if all those things were still to represent a small minority among them, we get to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> said, you don't really need a big number, you need just enough for the Garou to think it's not worth the trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T20:29:46-08:00","id":1555662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555649#post1555649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking everything the others said above, and want to add a few more:<br /> <br /> 1. Mages are interventionists by nature, even when they don't see what they're doing as intervention. They think they know better and have an innate power that literally validates this thinking. While a given Mage can certainly stop themselves from interfering for diplomatic reasons, they <b>do</b> think they have better ideas on how to deal with this sacred place, and very little regard for what others think. And not few of them will act upon their ideas sooner or later if they think they have an opportunity;<br /> <br /> 2. Even like-minded Mages don't necessarily have the exactly same worldview of the Garou, especially because <b>the Garou</b> also think themselves overly special. The simple idea of a non-shapechanger thinkering with the Caern in any way whatsoever isn't simply a risk, it pushes their buttons in all kinds of ways, in so many levels, because they're sure not only that this is a sacred place, but that they're the sacred race worthy of it and tasked with its care, them and no one else. They <i>barely</i> accept non-Garou shapechangers in the best days;<br /> <br /> 3. Not all Tradition Mages are that careful by a long shot. Like-minded Mages may agree that the Caern is a sacred place, but most Mages aren't like-minded, they're sympathetic at best. And with their &quot;know better&quot; attitude, a lot is far more pragmatic than respectful when push comes to shove, especially if it is to defend a cause they think worth it, which isn't necessarily in line with Garou perspective. Sure, only a <i>Nefandus</i> would destroy a Caern for no good reason, but far more Mages have reasons they disagree with Werewolves on how good they are.<br /> <br /> 4. Add to 3 that Garou are straight-up heroes, even if flawed ones, in the sense that they live to fight an undeniable evil over the world, but this evil is only undeniable in their eyes. Mages are <i><b>not</b></i> necessary heroes and <i><b>a lot</b></i> of them are not good people. Being a <i>Nefandus</i> means serving directly the kind of Evil the Garou fight, but below that anything goes and there are even Tradition Mages that are every bit the stereotyped luddite psychopathic asshole the Technocracy paints them. A lot of Tradition Mages do abhorrent things just because they don't think it that bad and don't really have to be good people anyways. Destroying a Caern is well within what many of them would do because they think they have better uses for that energy and Garou religion be damned;<br /> <br /> 5. Other Nodes exist, many others. There's zero need for the Garou to have their allies near the Caern or for those allies to ask. The mere fact of a Mage asking this would be reason to raise red flags far more than grant any privileges. Just why you want it? Under very extreme circumstances the Garou may invite them if it is to help with defending the Caern against certain destruction or a similarly extreme task, and even then only if they trust those Mages a lot and have reason to really think they may need this help (endangering the Caern out of pride is still its own crime), but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Even if all those things were still to represent a small minority among them, we get to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> said, you don't really need a big number, you need just enough for the Garou to think it's not worth the trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand all of that (although I disagree about Garou being more heroic than mages; Doc Eon, Porthos, Turing, and Dante are all better than Impergium and War of Rage fools), but the commenter I was replying to claimed that the Garou are &quot;frequently within reason&quot; to be paranoid about magi, and that magi actively go around draining Caerns. I'm not saying that Garou should let magi wander into Caerns, <b>I just want the receipts on that statement</b>. Which magi go around draining Caerns, which they view as a dying part of the natural magick of the world? <br /> <br /> It's not just morally wrong to drain a Caern, it's also completely moronic. As you said, there are other nodes, and a typical cabal probably has access to a node or a Chantry with a node. What does a typical cabal not have? The resources to fight their way through a pack of angry Garou in order to get at a Caern. Okay, maybe somebody invested a lot in the Wonder background; it's not <i>impossible</i> that a mage has access to an assault shotgun that creates flaming silver bullets or an eye that teleports whoever looks into it into a volcano or something. So, the magi gain a few more Quint. Okay. What did they lose? A chance to have a pack of Garou at their backs when dealing with Voormas's apprentice or something. I've heard of a cabal fighting to protect a Caern from BSDs, then leaving the Caern alone even though most of the Garou pack guarding it was devastated. On a related note, I've heard of a cabal spending ten game sessions in order to diplomatically circumvent an order from the Order of Hermes to take a Freehold, and uphold the status quo with the Changelings instead. I've never heard of a mystic cabal draining, moving, or cleansing a Caern/Freehold that wasn't held by BSDs or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T00:21:41-08:00","id":1555676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555662#post1555662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the commenter I was replying to claimed that the Garou are &quot;frequently within reason&quot; to be paranoid about magi, and that magi actively go around draining Caerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>That commenter was me, so let me explain.<br /> <br /> First, Garou are objectively heroes in their game line. Their whole society is dedicated to fight an objective evil. I'm not saying they're better or worse, much less that they don't do a lot of bad stuff, but as warriors fighting against the very spiritual force of corruption and destruction, they are heroes <i><b>as a society</b></i>, as far as one can be in the WoD. The Traditions don't exist for anything like this, they exist for self-defense. Mages <i><b>can</b></i> be good, just as Garou do, but pointing to specific individuals won't change that as a society this <i>isn't the point</i>. Not fighting for the greater good is a perfectly fine decision in Mage society, in Garou society it isn't.<br /> <br /> Second, you're focused on a <b><i>Mage</i></b> definition of <i>draining</i>, which isn't relevant here. I'm saying the Garou are within reason, but that's still from their perspective, and from their perspective any gathering of Quintessence or Tass is draining the Caern. What a Mage claims &quot;draining&quot; to be doesn't have any weight on what the Garou understand from a Mage sucking local Gnosis without a right to be there or regards for the state of the place before their arrival.<br /> <br /> Also, you're making an extreme interpretation of &quot;frequent within reason&quot;. It doesn't mean this happens every year or something, it doesn't means it is a majority of interactions, and it doesn't means what happens is exactly whatever the Garou worry about, it means something problematic enough for the Garou to see problems (and again, their perspective is what matters here) is frequent enough for the Garou to have reason to worry.<br /> <br /> Mages aren't only politically active Traditionalists, either, and the Garou can't really distinguish between them. All they know is that magic-wielding humans seek Caerns for Gnosis. Traditionalists, Technocrats, Crafts, Orphans, Nefandi, everything is the same for them, so they do have reason to worry since they can't know the Mages they're dealing with nor distinguish between factions very well.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, you're giving examples of PC cabals. PCs aren't representatives of the average fictional character, they are special. The Garou have reason because in the fiction of the setting it happens. If players actually do it is completely irrelevant, a lot of things that are extremely common for PCs are deemed rare occurrences in the lore. So those examples are kind of pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T06:15:24-08:00","id":1555681,"title":"","content":"There's also something that ties to the role of the Garou, and many mages would be unable to consider (even if not unwilling): There are unclaimed Caerns. They're rare, but they do exist. Mages that tap over an unclaimed Caern may not even know what they're doing. This increases the chance of them &quot;draining a Caern&quot; (whatever that means) unknowingly. <hr />So, there are many ways this could be spinned. There's a lot of things Mages can do to a Caern that could be the basis of the &quot;draining&quot; accusation. And there's a bunch of reasons I could imagine for mages to do it, from not knowing what they're doing, to scenarios of conflict.<br /> <br /> It's surely not a normal thing to happen, but I can see how it could have happened a few times. And that's enough to base a grudge because of how much of a &quot;holly cow&quot; Caerns are.<br /> <br /> It's true that the books never go deep into the particulars of such happenstances, tho. One would wish there was a bit more material arround this &quot;conflict&quot;, since it's supposed to be such a big deal, to flesh it out as more than just prejudice.<br /> <br /> But there's enough to build uppon, if one wishes to do the homework - so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T19:27:45-08:00","id":1555699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1555207-what-would-you-think-of-this-cabal-of-mages?p=1555681#post1555681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's surely not a normal thing to happen, but I can see how it could have happened a few times. And that's enough to base a grudge because of how much of a &quot;holly cow&quot; Caerns are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even because there's this very important aspect of how each view the situations where it happens, whatever it is.<br /> <br /> Tradition Mages may be against draining (as in completely depleting and destroying in the process) Nodes, especially Caerns, and some even may be wary of any other activity there the Garou would deem inappropriate. BUT...<br /> <br /> Mages don't have the well-being of Caerns in the very top of their priorities, and that's a <i>drastic</i> difference. There are many, many situations were a Mage would at least consider harming or even destroying a Caern for achieving a greater good (even putting aside the many Tradition Mages that don't give a fuck and would do so for personal gain and this <b>isn't</b> a crime for the Traditions and don't make them necessarily Nefandus). Indeed, a like-minded Mage may even conclude that the survival of the Garou at a Caern is more important than the Caern itself.<br /> <br /> Hardly will you find a Mage that could really say they would protect a Caern at absolutely any cost, or only concede to protect <i>even more</i> Caerns.<br /> <br /> But that's not how it works for Garou. Sure, they'll <b><i>sometimes</i></b> save themselves if they don't really hope to save the Caern, dying for a lost cause isn't <i>completely </i>mandatory. But if there's hope, even small, they'll give up as many lives as it takes. If the Caern survives at the cost of every last Garou, left to be claimed by some other werewolf or other Gaia servant, then that's a victory, full stop.<br /> <br /> So, when is it acceptable to compromise on one's ideals to battle a threat? Almost any Mage will have a far lower bar than the Garou when it comes to a Caern. And the WoD being what it is, even if this doesn't happen at the actual table, there's an implied history of such things happening. And the two sides don't talk enough to clarify misunderstandings, which is also important.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are Garou that break the rules. But they're seriously persecuted for this, and have a chance to live only because Gaia needs them, so they are an invaluable resource if they're able to not mess things up too much. Some will flee a Caern battle for thgeir lives, but they'll be forever remembered as untrustworthy cowards that only have to live because Gaia can still use their sorry asses for more than a Kinfolk would be able to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}